    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix Qwen3-Omni Thinker `lm_head` prefix propagation for the NVFP4\nquantization path.\n\nThis mirrors the related fix merged in\n[vllm-omni#4528](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-omni/pull/4528).\n\n## Claims\n\n- Pass the `lm_head` prefix to `ParallelLMHead`.\n- Prevent the BF16 `lm_head` from being incorrectly treated as an NVFP4\n  layer.\n- Fix the 1024-vs-2048 weight loading failure for Qwen3-Omni NVFP4\n  checkpoints.\n\n## Validation\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nExternal end-to-end validation was performed on a separate server with:\n\n- vLLM `0.29.0`\n- `vllm:v0.29.0`\n- RTX PRO 5000 72GB Blackwell GPU\n- `dizuo-ModelOpt-NVFP4` checkpoint\n\nBefore this change, loading failed with:\n\n```text\nRuntimeError: The size of tensor a (1024) must match\nthe size of tensor b (2048)\n```\n\nAfter this change:\n\n- The NVFP4 checkpoint loaded successfully.\n- All checkpoint shards loaded successfully.\n- `Application startup complete` was reached.\n- `/v1/models` reported `nvfp4`.\n- A 32-token completion returned valid Chinese text.\n\nThe external validation used the vLLM serving path with:\n\n```bash\nvllm serve <NVFP4_CHECKPOINT> \\\n  --served-model-name nvfp4 \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --max-model-len 32768 \\\n  --max-num-batched-tokens 32768 \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.92 \\\n  --block-size 128 \\\n  --enable-prefix-caching\n```\n\n## Details\n\n`Qwen3MoeLLMForCausalLM` constructed `ParallelLMHead` without passing its\nprefix. As a result, the ModelOpt NVFP4 exclusion rule could not match\n`lm_head`, and the BF16 head was incorrectly treated as an NVFP4 layer.\n\nThe fix passes `maybe_prefix(prefix, \"lm_head\")`, matching the existing\nQwen3 MoE implementation. The change is limited to one model constructor\nand does not alter behavior for other models or unquantized checkpoints.\n\nNo additional unit test was added because this failure requires a real\nNVFP4 checkpoint and quantized weight-loading path. The affected path was\nvalidated end to end on the required GPU environment.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
